NB. Initialize an empty stack (empty boxed list)
initStack =: 0 $ a:

NB. Check if stack is empty (returns 1 if empty, 0 otherwise)
isEmpty =: 0 = #

NB. Push an item onto the top of the stack (usage: item push stack)
push =: [ ,~ boxopen@]

NB. Peek at the top element without removing it
peek =: >@{.

NB. Pop the top element and return both (popped_item ; remaining_stack)
pop =: (>{.) ; }.

NB. Display stack elements from top to bottom
display =: echo

NB. ==========================================
NB. Example Usage
NB. ==========================================
s =: initStack ''
s =: 10 push s
s =: 20 push s
s =: 30 push s

display s                 NB. Output: ┌──┬──┬──┐ │30│20│10│ └──┴──┴──┘
echo 'Top item: ', ": peek s   NB. Output: Top item: 30

'popped s' =: pop s       NB. Unpacks popped value into 'popped' and updates 's'
echo 'Popped: ', ": popped     NB. Output: Popped: 30
display s                 NB. Output: ┌──┬──┐ │20│10│ └──┴──┘
echo 'Is empty: ', ": isEmpty s NB. Output: Is empty: 0
